.TH MEMEX-SEARCH 1 "August 2026" "memex 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memex-search \- search memex archives with PCRE2 patterns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memex search
.RI [ -i ]
.RI [ -w ]
.RI [ -F ]
.RI [ -m " N]"
.I PATTERN
.RI [ ARCHIVE ]
.PP
.B memex search
.RI [ -i ]
.RI [ -w ]
.RI [ -F ]
.RI [ -m " N]"
.B --service
.I FOLDER
.B --account
.I NAME
.I PATTERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memex search
searches mmap archives under
.BR ~/memex .
With no
.BR --service ,
no
.BR --account ,
and no archive path, the search is systemwide: every
.B *.majestic
under
.B $HOME/memex ,
leftover
.B *.archive
when there is no sibling same-stem
.BR .majestic .
Open maps the
.B .majestic
file with
.B PROT_READ
and
.BR MAP_SHARED .
That is a virtual mapping of the file, not a heap allocation of the file size.
Search reads that map. It does not copy the text blob into a
.BR Vec .
RSS is the pages the CPU has faulted, not the file size at mmap. The intended
page for text is 2 MiB. New ingest pads so text starts at a 2 MiB file offset.
A systemwide search maps all listed archives, holds those maps, compiles PCRE2
once, then runs PCRE2 on already-mapped text with min(file count, available
parallelism) workers. Search does not call
.B MADV_DONTNEED
after every archive while the search is still running. Hits are unique and
grouped by archive path, then conversation id. Default print cap is 100 unique
hits per archive.
It does not walk
.B $HOME
for live export dumps. Ingest owns discovery. It does not mmap
.BR .zst .
It does not spawn
.BR rg .
.PP
Search uses mmap text, grep-searcher, and grep-pcre2 only. Patterns are PCRE2
(the same engine as
.BR "rg -P" ).
There is no PCRE1 and no rust-regex fallback.
.PP
.B --service
and
.B --account
together, or an explicit archive path, search one file and do not scan home.
.PP
Durable search flags may be set in
.I ~/.config/majestic/memex.toml
under
.B [search]
.RI ( ignore_case ,
.IR fixed_strings ,
.IR word_regexp ,
.IR max_count ,
.IR archive ).
A missing file uses crate defaults (flags false, max_count 100, archive unset). CLI flags
override the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -i ", " --ignore-case
Case insensitive (Unicode).
.TP
.BR -w ", " --word-regexp
Whole word. Without
.BR -w ,
a match may sit inside a stored word.
.TP
.BR -F ", " --fixed-strings
Phrase or literal string.
.TP
.BR -m " N" ", " --max-count " N"
Unique hits printed per archive. Default 100. 0 means no cap.
.TP
.BI --service " FOLDER"
Folder under
.B $HOME/memex
(for example
.BR agents/grok ).
.TP
.BI --account " NAME"
Username file stem.
.SH SEARCH PATTERNS
.nf
Want                 Pattern
OR                   lizard|catfooding
AND, any order       (?=.*lizard)(?=.*the)
Phrase               'hello world'  or  -F 'hello world'
Case insensitive     -i
Whole word           -w
.fi
.PP
A
.B |
in the pattern is OR. AND any order uses lookaheads.
.B -i
is case insensitive.
.B -w
is whole word.
.B -F
is a phrase or literal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
memex search 'lizard|catfooding'
memex search '(?=.*lizard)(?=.*the)'
memex search -F 'hello world'
memex search -i catfooding
memex search -w food
memex search --service agents/grok --account personal PATTERN
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR memex (1)
